# netsurf: sibling combinators inside :not() / :is() / :where() are read as sibling rules (patch 505)
# Generated 2026-11-28
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 504)
#
# The sibling-rule scanner (patches 186/198/412/413/427) could not read a
# + or ~ inside a functional pseudo-class, and one such selector made its
# whole sheet conservative (state 2): every insert or removal anywhere on
# the page was then a sibling risk, answered by rebuilding the parent.
# stackoverflow's Stacks ".s-btn:not(.s-btn--radio:checked+label)..."
# (live here: patch 328 matches complex :not() arguments) made its flex
# <body> be rebuilt whole on each <iframe> it inserts.
#
# "X:not(A + B)" depends on X's previous sibling exactly as "A + B" does.
# When the prelude being parsed collects rules, html_rl_parse_prelude (now
# a wrapper of html_rl_parse_prelude1) points a scoped sink at fresh
# arrays; html_rl_parse_compound parses such an argument as a prelude of
# its own (html_rl_inner_arg) into the sink and then ignores the
# pseudo-class like a plain one -- a broader match, so more risk, never
# less. The wrapper moves the sink's rules, left compounds and :empty /
# :has() compounds into its caller's lists (a prelude holding one reports
# a sibling combinator) and frees them on a decline. An argument holding
# :has(), or one that does not parse, declines as before; calls that only
# scan (no rule list) see no sink and behave as before.
#
# Gate: JS-sib-not / CSS-sib-not-ref (six steps, row for row against the
# same steps at parse time). Its pair took the simulator gate's network
# page list to 385, past frontends/vita/main.c's VITA_NET_PAGES_MAX: raised
# 384 -> 512 (static tables, ~152 KiB).
--- a/content/handlers/html/html.c
